# 5. Notes on System Requirements

## Vision

Develop an AI-assisted triage system that combines handwritten patient information and automatically collected vital signs to support nurses in making faster and more accurate triage decisions.

---

## Inputs

### Patient Information

* Patient demographics
* Chief complaint
* Medical history
* Handwritten symptoms
* Pain score
* Existing EHR data

### Smart Pen Data

* Digital handwriting
* Heart-rate estimate
* Grip pressure
* Tremor detection
* Writing speed and pauses
* Initial skin-temperature reading

### Connected Device Data

* Blood pressure
* Heart rate
* Oxygen saturation
* Clinical temperature
* Weight

---

## Outputs

* Digital copy of the patient’s handwriting
* Structured patient record
* Predicted ESI level
* Confidence score
* Critical alerts
* Explanation of contributing factors
* Missing or unreliable data warnings
* Audit log

---

## Integration Requirements

* Integrates with the hospital Electronic Health Record.
* Links the Smart Pen to the correct patient using a barcode, wristband, or patient identifier.
* Receives vital signs from connected medical devices.
* Links each device reading to the correct patient record.
* Converts handwriting into structured digital text while preserving the original handwriting.
* Sends the AI prediction directly to the nurse dashboard.
* Clearly separates patient-reported information, measured vital signs, and AI-generated recommendations.
* Allows the nurse to accept, request more information, or override the AI recommendation.
* Records all predictions and nurse actions in an audit log.
* Stores patient data securely.
* Supports a manual workflow if the pen, network, or connected devices fail
* Provides a colour-blind accessibility mode and uses text, symbols, and labels alongside colour-coded alerts.

